WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.477
This code creates a simple class called CustomerRecord.

00:00:03.477 --> 00:00:07.002
The class has a special method called __init__.

00:00:07.002 --> 00:00:10.202
This method runs when a new object is created.

00:00:10.202 --> 00:00:15.342
It receives customer_id and segment and stores them inside the object.

00:00:15.342 --> 00:00:19.677
The word self refers to the specific object being created.

00:00:19.677 --> 00:00:26.137
When we write self.customer_id, we are storing the customer ID inside that object.

00:00:26.137 --> 00:00:31.807
When we write self.segment, we are storing the segment inside that same object.

00:00:31.807 --> 00:00:34.857
Then we create one object called customer.

00:00:34.857 --> 00:00:38.892
We pass in the values C101 and Retail.

00:00:38.892 --> 00:00:42.877
After that, we print customer.customer_id and customer.segment.

00:00:42.877 --> 00:00:45.067
Before running the cell, predict what it will print.

00:00:45.067 --> 00:00:51.392
It should print the customer ID and the segment stored in that object.

00:00:51.392 --> 00:00:58.907
After running the code, try creating another customer object with a different ID and segment.

00:00:58.907 --> 00:01:04.160
This will help you see that the class is the blueprint, and each object stores its own data.
